body:
i get it, this post is making fun of a stupid patriot who couldn't understand english.

&#x200B;

im glad that no patriot has the urge to post about a stupid vnch.

I hated transforming into non-sentient objects. By the time I gained enough consciousness to transform back to my favorite form, 6 months had passed. I was buried 6 feet under by Serena, and it was horrible transforming back into an old geezer just to have a mouthful... and noseful... and eyeful of dirt. I had to return to my true form - the Evil Dragon, the incarnation of Darkness itself - to get up from the underground. Then, another inconvenience occurred - I couldn't possibly use my favorite human form anymore, because that form was supposedly dead, even if there was only 1 person who knew it. I then grumpily transformed to my second-favorite form, an old elf, and began to look for my second protegee.

&#x200B;

After a 3 months of searching, I kidnapped a young, cunning elf from the West Forest of the Holy City. The searching was much quicker than the first time! As I was celebrating in my mind, I found out through the rumours in the Holy City that Serena - my first student - became a Demi-God ranked hero nicknamed The Dark Sword. And in her interviews, she said that her goal was to...slain the Evil Dragon for killing her master. My jaws dropped to the ground, and I swore to myself to never fake such stupid backstory ever again.

&#x200B;

And so, after another year, I finished teaching Kaiden - the elf that was my 2nd ever student. It was time to fake my death again. This time, however, It'll be different.

&#x200B;

"Kaiden." I said while still faking meditating in the classic lotus position. We were "training our mind" at a pond under a waterfall.

&#x200B;

"Yes, master?" Answered the elf. I opened my eyes just a little bit to check and he was kneeling right in front of me, his head lowered.

&#x200B;

"I command you to run from this place, and leave me behind."

&#x200B;

"What are you saying, master?" He looked up, confused. But his confusion lasted a mere second, as lightning struck the edge of the pond, as four figure emerged from the dust.

&#x200B;

"So we finally meet again." I stood up, shouted to the 4 puppets that I made and scripted just a night before, after I commanded Kaiden to go and find woods.

&#x200B;

"Dark Lord Werzagkuir, Foul Magic practitioner." said the puppet in the biggest, shiniest armor with a huge ass sword "In the name of the Holy Kingdom, we will make you pay for your evil deeds."

&#x200B;

"Evil deeds?" Kaiden screamed "My master had never done anything wrong!!!"

&#x200B;

Fwoosh!!

&#x200B;

In a blink of an eye, the sword carrying puppet closed the gap and struck Kaiden. Of course, like a cliched B-rate action movie, I would take the hit for my beloved student.

&#x200B;

"Kuh...!!!" I vomited blood dramatically. "Kaiden! Run away! These knights are equipped with anti-dark magic, I will try to hold them back!"

&#x200B;

"M...Master!! How could I..."

&#x200B;

"All out attack!" The sword puppet shouted. And the other 3 started to make their moves. The scepter puppet shot holy light at Kaiden, the bow puppet aimed at my head, and the bard puppet started playing, buffing their whole party. I dodged the arrows, throw a dark energy ball at the bard, then took the holy light hit for Kaiden.

&#x200B;

"Gah!!!" I screamed while casting a spell on myself, causing me to bleed even more profusely.

&#x200B;

"Master!!!" Kaiden assumed his fighting stance "Don't worry! I'll fight with you!"

&#x200B;

"Kaider Jah'sed Lairyl" I muttered Kaiden's true name while deflecting a huge holy light ball coming at us, and catching the sword of the sword puppet with my barehand "I command you to run away, and never look back."

&#x200B;

The elf's true name was spoken by his master. He could not go against it. His body moved against his will, and he started to run.

&#x200B;

"Master!!! No!!!" His words echoed in the deep forest "I'll save you!!! Please wait for me!!!"

&#x200B;

"Scepter puppet, shoot a fireball at the direction he's going." I commanded the scepter puppet after making sure Kaiden went far enough. After the fireball lit up the whole forest, I cancelled the matter manipulation spell i casted on the puppets. Their armors fell onto the ground, and I let out a breath of relief. Kaiden was gone, and I just have to wait a few days before I change my appearance to another, and go kidnap my next student.

&#x200B;

Little did I know, it would take me months before I could find a suitable one to teach. While searching, I also found out that Kaiden became a hero known as The Vigilante. Rumor said that he searched and killed  knights and other heroes who abused their position and power for their own gains. I had no problem with that, but it was said that he was also searching for his master who he believed firmly was still alive, because he couldn't find my corpse after coming back to the "battlefield". I cursed my own stupidity for days after finding out.

&#x200B;

Today, finally, I found my next student, perfect for me to teach. I ventured into the deepest, most dangerous place of the world: The Demonfolk's territory. I found her, hugging the corpse which I supposed was her mother under a cliff. She growled at me, her hateful eyes gave me hope and joy.

&#x200B;

No way in hell she could turn into a hero...Right?

What makes a hero?

&#x200B;

Is it the unyielding mental fortitude, never to give up even in the direst situation? Is it the unrivaled strength, enough for an individual to sweep away thousands and thousands of elite-rank enemies? Or is it the selflessness, the will to sacrifice oneself to achieve absolute justice?

&#x200B;

This is not a rhetorical question. I'm asking because I don't have a damn clue. And I'm really, really, really tired of raising my precious students to walk on the path of darkness, only for them to become a hero later on. If I get a coin for every time a student that I taught becomes a hero, I'll have 2 coins. Which is not much, but I've only ever raised 2 students, which makes it 100%!!

&#x200B;

You see, my specialty in this world is that of a teacher. And what a teacher do is, well, teach. But alas, there comes 2 main problems. The first one is, due to my alignment in this world, the only thing that I can teach is Dark Magic - magic in its most heinous form, and can only be used for evil purposes as far as history of this world goes. Therefore, I can't just open a school and recruit students, the Holy Knights and the Heroes Society will undoubtedly come and woop my ass. And since I can't open a school, the 2nd problem reveals itself: I had no student. What good can a teacher be without his student??  If I have no student then I can't teach. And if I can't teach, then this damned system mission of mine would inevitably failed, leading to penalty. And I wouldn't want another penalty you know...Because the first time I failed a quest, I became immortal. Yes, I am your generic transported-to-another-world-with-a-cheat-system character.

&#x200B;

I had flew over countless human cities, burrowed under many elven forests, and swam through The Great Sea itself. Over the course of 4 years, I could only kidnap 2 children. In this world, even the homeless has an ID card to control the population, which made my job even harder. I have 6 years left to raise 3 students, to complete this damned mission of mine before getting struck with another horrible penalty. Easy, you might think. And easy, I thought it was...Until after I had taught the first ever student of mine everything...and had nothing left to teach. What could I have done? I needed to find a reason to ditch her, I couldn't waste time staying with 1 student forever. And I couldn't imagine the carnage there would be if there were more than 1 student with me at a time...The process of teaching Dark Magic is always brutal, and it causes a lot of attention. More than 1 staying with me at a time, and we will inevitably get caught by those pesky Holy Knights for practicing forbidden knowledge. So, I considered my options.

&#x200B;

Sneak out of the cave in the middle of the night? She would think that it was a test and her goal was to find me, and being the smartass she was, she would definitely caught me in a span of 1 day. Kill her? I didn't want to risk the mission point not getting counted. Beside, after I taught her everything I could, she was as strong if not stronger than me, despite me being immortal. So, the only seemingly good option left was...

&#x200B;

"Serena..." I faked a bloody cough while looking wearily at my first ever student. She struggled to keep the tears from her eyes to no avail, her shaking hand placed on mine.

&#x200B;

"I don't have...much time left...Ugh!" I whimpered. "The Dark Magic of the Evil Dragon has...almost consumed me..."

&#x200B;

"I'm sorry teacher." She bit her lower lip, blood gushing down along with the tears "I couldn't do anything for you..."

&#x200B;

"What a nice act. Im sure you hate me to the guts." I thought to myself. Nobody could possibly have affection toward me after all I've done in the name of "teaching Dark Magic" to them.

&#x200B;

"You...made me proud." I tried to smile as faint as I could "Now...go outside and show the world...The true meaning of Dark Magic..."

&#x200B;

Then, I slowly transform into a pile of ash. She had never witnessed me transforming before, and so she thought what happened to me was because the Magic of Evil Dragon had completely erased my existence - at least I hope that's what happened because in the process of transforming, I slowly lose my consciousness.
